# ---------------- OP Mainnet
P(10,'L1','Karst is the active fork and Lagoon has no date in the registry. The official endpoint still reports a build without a version, so two client fixes of the last three months cannot be tied to the sequencer build.',[
 D('The hardfork registry lists Karst as active since 8 July 2026 (timestamp 1783526401) and Lagoon as in development with no activation. Karst brought EIP-7825 (16,777,216 gas per transaction, deposits exempt), EIP-7823, EIP-7883, EIP-7939 and EIP-7951 to L2. An eth_call that runs opcode 0x1e (CLZ) on the value 1 returned 255 on all seven endpoints of this unit, so the Osaka instruction set is live on each of them.','https://docs.optimism.io/op-stack/protocol/network-upgrades','low'),
 D('op-reth v2.4.3 of 8 September 2026 rejects deposit (0x7E) and post-execution (0x7D) transactions that arrive as a bare RLP body without the type byte. The pull request states that the missing byte could bypass the leading-byte transaction gates of derivation. A deposit carries no signature and may carry a mint, so the gate is what stops a batch author from placing one in a batch.','https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/pull/22778','low'),
 D('A trie iterator fault in reth (fixed upstream on 3 November 2026) can drop a leaf from an incremental state root. Fixed builds are reth v2.10.0, op-reth v2.8.1 and Base v1.5.3. The advisory reports stalls and wrong eth_getProof answers and no loss of funds.','https://www.0xcert.com/advisory/0xCERT-2026-0317','low')])
P(10,'L2','The one transaction-boundary fault found in this family in 2026 left warm account entries of a rejected transaction in the journal. The op-revm handler at the release that three sibling chains report discards the journal on every transaction error.',[
 D('The handler of op-revm at tag op-reth/v2.9.0-rc.1 contains journal discard_tx calls on the error path. The page of the Base fix of June 2026 lists a referencing pull request numbered 21723 with the title fix(op-revm): discard journal after non-deposit tx errors (SDM warm-set leak). Which build the OP Mainnet sequencer runs is still unknown.','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/op-reth/v2.9.0-rc.1/rust/op-revm/src/handler.rs','low')])
P(10,'L3','A single transaction can still sweep the deepest ETH and USDC pool of this PoolManager far below the gas cap. The base fee read from chain was 10,576 wei.',[
 D('The deployed Quoter reports 1,914,692 gas for an exact input swap of 10^30 wei of ETH in the ETH and USDC pool with fee 500 and tick spacing 10, which empties the USDC side (20,505.5 USDC out). That is 11 percent of the 16,777,216 gas cap. The latest block had gas limit 40,000,000 and gas used 25,297,791.','https://mainnet.optimism.io','low')])
P(10,'L4','No interop predeploy has an implementation yet, on OP Mainnet or on OP Sepolia.',[
 D('The EIP-1967 implementation slot of 0x4200000000000000000000000000000000000022 to 0x4200000000000000000000000000000000000030 is zero at block 159,927,264 except at 0x2c and 0x2d, which hold the implementations recorded in cycle 5. On OP Sepolia at block 51,825,395 the same slots are zero with the same two exceptions, so Lagoon has not installed code on the testnet either.','https://mainnet.optimism.io','low')])

# ---------------- Base
P(8453,'L1','Base enforces the 16,777,216 gas cap since Azul and runs a precompile set of its own. Two precompiles that earlier profiles did not sweep, the transaction context and the nonce manager, are installed since Cobalt and are read only.',[
 D('In the node source at v1.5.6 the precompile provider installs, from Cobalt on, TxContext at 0x813000000000000000000000000000000000aa02 and NonceManager at 0x813000000000000000000000000000000000aa01 next to the B20 factory, the token lookup, the policy registry and the activation registry. TxContext has three getters that fall back to tx.origin outside a type 0x79 transaction, and NonceManager exposes getNonce only.',B+'provider.rs','low'),
 D('The Beryl review of the precompiles (Cantina, report dated 14 August 2026) has one high finding: input one byte above the size limit of the BN254 pairing and BLS12-381 precompiles returned a fatal error that could fail block execution. At v1.5.6 the pairing guard returns a precompile halt, which is an ordinary failed call.','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/base/base/main/audits/beryl/beryl-b20.pdf','low'),
 D('The throughput page states a protocol maximum of 16,777,216 gas per transaction since Azul, 40,000,000 gas per block and five blocks per second on mainnet, and a deposit limit of 20,000,000 gas per L1 block.','https://docs.base.org/specifications/transactions/throughput-and-limits.md','low')])
P(8453,'L2','The two block production halts of 25 and 26 June 2026 came from journal state that the block builder kept after a rejected transaction. The fix is in the handler of the release that runs today.',[
 D('The postmortem states that an invalid transaction failed in the block builder without clearing the journal of accessed accounts and slots, that the next valid transaction was charged different gas, and that validators recomputed the block with a clean journal, found another receipts root and rejected it. Block production stopped for 116 and for 20 minutes.','https://www.base.org/blog/postmortem-june-25th-block-production-outage.md','high'),
 D('Pull request 3806 adds a discard of the journal for every error that is not a failed deposit. In crates/common/evm/src/handler.rs at v1.5.6 the function catch_error commits the journal for a failed deposit (line 377) and calls discard_tx in every other case (line 386).','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/base/base/v1.5.6/crates/common/evm/src/handler.rs','low')])
P(8453,'L3','The transfer policies of the two B20 tokens with the largest PoolManager balances are block lists that one externally owned account each administers. The PoolManager passes all of them today.',[
 D('OUSD 0xB2000000000000000000002fEb517dFeC7415344 (PoolManager balance 5,319,114.88 at block 61,314,282) binds TRANSFER_SENDER_POLICY to policy 0x7a, a block list whose admin is 0x251d2711ebeb0a09fdb8992f5506f3d949175246, an account without code. Its five other policy scopes hold policy 0, the built in policy that authorizes every account. AMDc 0xb2000000000000000000000d8ce462e99ee7a47b binds sender, receiver, executor and mint receiver to block list 5 (admin 0xec0f05c174e54fbf0fe16ad930a8afebce612812, no code) and seize exempt to block list 0x81 (admin 0x38467be00970af18076fd08f6b4cf38ba91572b1, no code). isAuthorized returns true for the PoolManager on each.','https://mainnet.base.org/','high'),
 D('The deployed Quoter reports 3,982,297 gas for an exact input swap of 10^30 wei of ETH in the ETH and USDC pool with fee 500 and tick spacing 10 (86,156.9 USDC out), which is 24 percent of the gas cap.','https://mainnet.base.org/','low')])
P(8453,'L4','Every Base precompile address was called through a forwarding stub at the PoolManager address with the sixteen call shapes. Only transfer and balanceOf on created B20 tokens return, and every call with value reverts.',[
 D('Factory 0xB20f000000000000000000000000000000000000, policy registry 0x8453000000000000000000000000000000000002, activation registry 0x8453000000000000000000000000000000000001, TxContext and NonceManager revert on empty calldata, on empty calldata with 1 wei (error 0x6fb1b0e9), on transfer, on balanceOf, on the ten hook selectors and on unlockCallback. OUSD and AMDc return true for transfer of 0 and of 1 and return the balance for balanceOf, and revert on the other shapes. A B20 shaped address that was never created reverts on every shape.','https://mainnet.base.org/','low'),
 D('The Beryl review found that the factory accepted value on calls to nonpayable selectors and stranded it (fixed), and the Cobalt review found the same for the activation registry (fixed). The dispatch of the stablecoin variant at v1.5.6 rejects a nonzero call value with NonPayable before it decodes calldata.',B+'b20_stablecoin/dispatch.rs','low')])

